.env
.env.local

# Google ADK local dev artefacts
demo/*/.venv/
demo/**/.adk/session.db

# In-cluster zot registry cache mirrored to the host during push-local.
# Files under .cache/zot/ are written by the zot container as UID 65532 and
# are unreadable by git (status chokes on .cache/zot/acme/). Local-only.
.cache/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# .DS_Store
.DS_Store

# Node dependencies
node_modules/

# Playwright storage-state / auth artifacts (session material — never commit)
test/acceptance/.auth/

# wait.sh is a vendored source lib, not a build artifact — override the global `lib` ignore
!scripts/lib/
!scripts/lib/**

# Same override, same reason: ~/.gitignore_global carries a bare `lib` pattern
# (a Python packaging leftover) which silently swallows ANY directory named lib
# at any depth. test/lib/ holds detik.bash, linter.bash, utils.bash, and
# fake-image-cli.bash — without this negation new helpers there are never
# committed.
!test/lib/
!test/lib/**

# Embedded BPF bytecode objects: override ~/.gitignore_global `*.o` rule so
# bpf_embed.go has its object present in fresh worktrees without rebuilding.
!d2-signalloom/apps/signalloom-warden/pkg/tc/tc_drop.bpf.o


# riskctl build output (regenerate with `make riskctl`)
tools/riskctl/riskctl

# Public tunnel state (make public / make public-down)
.tunnel/
tunnel-policy.yaml

# Session artifacts (PAI work memory, plans, CI reports, test results)
MEMORY/
Plans/
lane-reports*/
# Written by scripts/gcp-tf/demo-up.sh. Covers demo-reports/ and the
# demo-reports.prev/ generation it rotates the previous run into.
demo-reports*/
# Also written by scripts/gcp-tf/demo-up.sh: one receipt per lane per test
# surface, read by `make gcp-tf-test-surfaces`.
#
# A SIBLING of demo-reports/ rather than a directory inside it, deliberately:
# rotate_reports() moves REPORT_DIR wholesale to .prev at the start of every
# on-VM run, so a receipt filed in there would be carried off by the next run
# and the both-surfaces verdict would report a surface that had just passed as
# never having run.
#
# Ignoring it is NOT cosmetic. demo-up.sh refuses to deliver from a dirty tree,
# so an untracked receipt here makes the very next `demo-up.sh up` refuse —
# which is exactly what test/terraform-demo-driver.bats caught when this
# directory was first added without this line.
demo-surfaces*/
d2-signalloom/results.tap
results.tap
*.tap
test/gcp-results/
test/gcp-5x-results.md
# supercred-e2e.sh writes one .state snapshot and .log per assertion point here
# (31 files for a 5-iteration run), and Playwright drops traces here too. The
# block above claimed to cover "test results" and did not.
test-results/
# scripts/jev-test-bot/loop.sh writes one directory per exploration run here
# (routes.txt, dashboard.log, iteration-N.json, iteration-N-areas/*.json with
# one file per route, summary.json). A 44-route single iteration is ~50 files,
# and the run's scratch and browser-profile directories live inside it too
# while the run is live — so this is per-run evidence, never source.
#
# Same reasoning as demo-surfaces/ above and not cosmetic: several scripts in
# this repo refuse to act on a dirty tree, so an untracked run directory here
# would make the next one of those refuse.
reports/
test/local-5x-results.md
# >>> terraform (F1-foundation) >>>
# Terraform lock files are deliberately committed so everyone resolves the same provider build.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/
# Terraform can create named local cache directories (for example .terraform-demo-1).
.terraform*/
# Saved execution plans are generated local artifacts and may contain sensitive values.
*.tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
!*.example.tfvars
# <<< terraform (F1-foundation) <<<

# >>> gcp deploy inputs and hand-off (I1-v2-make-handoff) >>>
# Everything under deploy/gcp/ that is not documentation names the real estate.
#
# The hand-off is generated by `make gcp-tf-handoff` and read by the test code.
# It carries the project id, the deploy service account, the instance name and
# the VM's internal IP — a complete map of a live, billable estate. It is
# regenerable from state in one command, so committing it buys nothing and
# leaks everything.
deploy/gcp/*.handoff.json
# One line: the email of the service account Terraform impersonates. The email
# contains the project id.
deploy/gcp/deploy-sa
# The destroy-preservation baseline, written by `scripts/gcp-tf/preserve-check.sh
# --capture` and read back by the same script after a destroy. It carries NO
# secret material by construction -- only bucket names, object counts per state
# prefix, secret version counts and service account emails -- but every one of
# those names embeds the real project id, which CONTRACT.md §6 keeps out of
# committed files. Regenerate it with --capture rather than committing it.
deploy/gcp/preserve-baseline.json
# Saved plan files. A plan is a binary diff against one specific state serial;
# committing one invites applying a diff that no longer describes reality.
*.tfplan
# Per-environment Terraform data dirs. `.terraform/` above does not match these:
# each environment gets its own `.terraform-<env>/`, which holds the resolved
# backend pointer and the saved plan file.
.terraform-*/
# <<< gcp deploy inputs and hand-off (I1-v2-make-handoff) <<<

# A .terraform.lock.hcl is only consulted in a ROOT module. In a shared child
# module it is inert, and it silently drifts from whatever the roots actually
# lock — so a reviewer reading modules/network/.terraform.lock.hcl learns
# nothing true. Roots commit theirs (ISC-13); child modules must not.
terraform/modules/*/.terraform.lock.hcl

# Sentinels dropped by the mutation-proof harnesses while a REAL file is
# deliberately broken, and removed when they restore. CONTRACT §7b requires
# mutating the real tree, so an interrupted run leaves the repository mutated;
# the harness REFUSES to start when it finds one of these rather than repairing,
# which is the signal that matters. Ignored so a `git add -A` inside that window
# cannot commit the sentinel and make the refusal permanent.
#
# They survive SIGKILL, and that is the point: a tool timeout escalates to
# SIGKILL, no trap survives it, and a leaked mutation then reads as a genuine
# regression on the next run. Measured on 2026-08-20 — a killed gate left
# `[ "${FORCE:-0}" != "1" ] || force=1` replaced by `:` and the following run
# reported it as content lost in a merge.
#
# A PATTERN rather than one line per harness, and each harness must choose a
# name UNIQUE TO ITSELF. A shared sentinel is worse than none: harness A's
# restore deletes harness B's in-progress marker, so B's next run sees a clean
# repo, reads B's own leaked mutation as a real failure, and the refusal that
# was supposed to catch it never fires.
*mutation-in-progress

# The saved KubeSec-AFM image, produced by `scripts/k8s-afm.sh save` and
# delivered to a lane by scripts/gcp-tf/demo-up.sh:deliver_afm_image.
#
# Gitignored deliberately and load-bearingly. The lane payload is
# `git archive HEAD` — tracked files only — and that property is the security
# boundary of the whole lane, not an optimisation: it is what guarantees no
# tfvars, no .keys and no hand-off can ride along. Tracking a 245MB image here
# would put a binary blob inside that boundary and add ~7x to every payload.
# The archive travels as its OWN scp, next to the payload, never inside it.
.afm-image/

# Bun temporary files
d2-signalloom/bun/


# Editor session logs
.nvimlog
# Kanban runtime state written into task worktrees by the runtime.
# Without this, every card preflight sees `?? .kanban/objectives.json` and fails
# its clean-tree gate, because the card is forbidden from touching runtime state.
.kanban/

# In-repo Claude agent worktrees (blocked by scripts/check-worktree-hygiene.sh;
# ignored so legacy worktrees <= 21 days old do not pollute git status or search tools).
.claude/worktrees/

# Project skills: `.claude/skills` is a committed symlink to `.agents/skills`,
# so Claude Code discovers every repo skill without per-user links. The
# re-include beats a global `.claude/` ignore (repo .gitignore outranks
# core.excludesFile). Everything else under .claude/ stays ignored.
!.claude/
.claude/*
!.claude/skills

# Local kind cluster state: regenerated by every `kind create`, points at an
# ephemeral localhost port, and carries client key material. Never commit.
.kind/

# parallel-acceptance.sh output root if ever pointed into the tree
.parallel-acceptance/

# SLSI-P1-1: bundle binary layout (staged multi-arch binaries ignored; checksums and versions committed)
bundle/bin/*/*
!bundle/bin/*/versions.txt
!bundle/bin/checksums.txt

# SLSI-P1-2: offline OCI image layout (blobs, staging directories, signatures, and archives ignored)
bundle/images/oci/blobs/
bundle/images/.staging*
bundle/images/*.tar
bundle/images/*.tar.gz
bundle/images/signatures/
bundle/images/flux/charts/*.tgz

# SLSI-P1-3: bundle distribution archives and manifests
dist/
